{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104556","id":2414102294,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6P5EcW","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104556","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104556.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104556.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104556","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104556/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104556/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104556/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ffa6ef220bdefe64b0d2ebb3c48c5dc54d52045b","number":104556,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use `append_` instead of `parse_` for `String` methods.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`String` has various methods like `parse_utf8`. These functions replace the current contents of the string with the contents of a buffer of some encoding.\r\nThis PR expands versatility of these methods, to be able to append to existing contents. This makes them more versatile, exemplified by the ability to remove 3 functions of duplicated functionality in `ustring.cpp`.\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\n`parse_` function behavior is somewhat odd: The old string isn't used at all - instead, its contents are fully replaced. \r\nIt is questionable whether it wouldn't be a better fit to just create a new string.\r\n\r\nIndeed, most callers look like this:\r\n```c++\r\nString new_string;\r\nnew_string.parse_utf8(utf8_buffer);\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis would be more idiomatic with the factory method:\r\n```c++\r\nString new_string = String::utf8(utf8_buffer);\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese cases make up a good ~80% of `parse_` callers.\r\nAnother ~15% actually does something with the error:\r\n```c++\r\nString new_string;\r\nERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(new_string.parse_utf8(utf8_buffer), \"Failed to parse string.\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis would be equivalent to calling `append_` functions:\r\n```c++\r\nString new_string;\r\nERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(new_string.append_utf8(utf8_buffer), \"Failed to parse string.\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nFinally, there are only a handful of callers that actually want to replace the string in question:\r\n```c++\r\nthis->string.parse_utf8(utf8_buffer);\r\n```\r\n\r\nThey need the (slightly awkward) workaround of clearing the string first:\r\n```c++\r\nthis->string.clear();\r\nthis->string.append_utf8(utf8_buffer);\r\n// Alternatively, this->string = String::utf8(utf8_buffer);\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlright, so \"replace\" functionality is not used often, so what?\r\nI'd argue that `append_` functionality is useful more often: Basically, append the contents of the buffer to the existing contents. This allows them to be used when combining buffers / string parts, which currently is often performed using the rather slow `+` operator.\r\nDe-duplication potential can be seen immediately because `operator+=` functions can be re-implemented by calling `append_`. I may eventually make a follow-up proposal to replace uses of `operator+=` with `append_` calls, because it makes the expected type of encoding more explicit.\r\n\r\nIn addition, these functions will be usable for `String::concat` eventually (#99929). This will require a few more changes, but this is a necessary refactor step going in the right direction. :)\r\n\r\n## Caveats\r\nThere is one performance benefit of `parse_xxx`: If there was a previous string of similar length, the existing buffer may be reusable, saving time allocating a new one.\r\n\r\nHowever, given how few callers even use `parse_` for replacing strings, I think this is not important. In addition, this problem would be better solved by implementing `reserve()` for `CowData`, allowing for non-deallocating resize. I am planning to propose this functionality when I make progress with other `CowData` changes.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","